import Mathlib
import Catalog.Novelty.FibCarmichaelStructure

/-!
# Local-to-global structure of the Fibonacci rank of apparition

This file is a **sheaf-theoretic / local-to-global** reading of the Fibonacci entry-point
(rank-of-apparition) theory developed in
`Catalog/Novelty/FibonacciEntryPointDuality.lean` (the master duality
`fib_dvd_iff_fibEntry_dvd : p ∣ F n ↔ z(p) ∣ n`) and
`Catalog/Novelty/FibCarmichaelStructure.lean` (totality `exists_pos_fib_dvd`/`fibEntry_pos`,
the meet law `fib_dvd_gcd_iff`, the binary lcm law `fibEntry_coprime_mul`, its finite
pairwise-coprime generalization `fibEntry_prod_coprime`, and the squarefree specialization
`fibEntry_squarefree`).

The unifying idea: for each modulus `p` the **divisibility set** `U(p) = {n | p ∣ F n}` is
*exactly* the principal ideal generated by the entry point `z(p) = fibEntry p`
(`fib_divisibility_principal`).  Thus `z` is a complete **local invariant**: knowing the single
number `z(p)` ("the stalk at `p`") recovers the entire global divisibility section `U(p)`.  The
lattice morphism laws of `z` then become *gluing* statements, and the failure of strict
multiplicativity becomes a *cocycle / overlap* term measured by a gcd.

## Main results

* `fib_divisibility_principal` — **stalk = principal ideal.** `{n | p ∣ F n} = {n | z(p) ∣ n}`.
  The local datum `z(p)` is a complete invariant of the global section.
* `fibEntry_eq_lcm_primePow` — **global gluing from prime-power stalks.** For every `n > 0`,
  `z(n) = lcm_{p ∣ n} z(p^{v_p(n)})`.  This sharpens `fibEntry_squarefree` from squarefree `n`
  to *arbitrary* `n`: the entry point is glued from its values on the prime-power "charts".
* `fib_prod_dvd_iff_forall` — **local sections glue.** For a pairwise-coprime family `f` on a
  finset `s`, the product modulus `∏ f i` divides `F n` iff every local modulus `f i` does.
* `fibEntry_coprime_obstruction` — **overlap cocycle.** For coprime `m, n`,
  `z(m) · z(n) = z(m·n) · gcd(z(m), z(n))`.  The deviation of `z` from being multiplicative is
  exactly the gcd overlap term — the obstruction to gluing local entry points into a strict
  product.

## Catalog synthesis

Every result here is built on the catalog: `fib_divisibility_principal` is the set-level form of
`FibEntryDuality.fib_dvd_iff_fibEntry_dvd`; `fibEntry_eq_lcm_primePow` is
`FibCarmichaelStructure.fibEntry_prod_coprime` applied to the prime-power factorisation
(`Nat.factorization_prod_pow_eq_self`), strictly generalising
`FibCarmichaelStructure.fibEntry_squarefree`; `fib_prod_dvd_iff_forall` reuses the duality plus
coprime product divisibility; and `fibEntry_coprime_obstruction` combines
`FibCarmichaelStructure.fibEntry_coprime_mul` with `Nat.gcd_mul_lcm`.

